    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm looking for some help with my Monstera deliciosa. It's been sitting in my living room for a year and doing great, but lately, the lower leaves are starting to turn a pale yellow color. The soil feels kind of damp even when I think I've watered it, but I don't see any obvious pests. Any idea what might be going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pale yellowing leaves on your Monstera deliciosa, though not due to pests, might be caused by overwatering. Monstera plants prefer the soil to be only slightly moist, not damp, and excess moisture can lead to root rot. Consider reducing your watering frequency and ensuring that the pot has good drainage to prevent water from accumulating at the bottom.",
