      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pale yellow and mottled spots on your Monstera's leaves might be a sign of insufficient nutrients, and fertilizing your plant might help. Monstera deliciosa benefits from regular feeding with a balanced, water-soluble fertilizer, especially during their growing season (spring and summer) when they are the most active. Be sure to follow the instructions for the fertilizer, as over-fertilizing can exacerbate the issue of root rot by promoting excessive growth of delicate root systems susceptible to rot. Always water the plant well after applying fertilizer and ensure it is in well-draining soil to prevent further complications.",
