    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While lack of light can cause some yellowing or etching on leaves as the plant attempts to photosynthesize in insufficient light, it's unlikely that the poor lighting conditions in one part of your room would be the sole cause of the symptoms you've described. Considering the various possibilities, it's essential to look at the plant from multiple angles and check localized issues. The corner might have factors like lower humidity levels, temperature variations, or even micro-environmental stresses which impact the plant's condition there. Another possibility is that the new plantings next to your Monstera, or even the mere proximity to the wall leading to less airflow and transpiration, could have contributed. It's best to research each suspect until your Monstera's health stabilizes. Balance the environmental factors for optimal growth and consider a more evenly distributed light source if light is indeed a concern.",
